/*Q24. A company evaluates an employee's monthly performance based on the number of tasks completed. The evaluation process must calculate a
performance score and temporarily revise the task count without modifying the original number of completed tasks.
Write a Java program using the EmployeePerformance class to demonstrate method calls, return values, and pass-by-value for primitive
data types.
Implement the following static methods inside the EmployeePerformance class:
int calculateScore(int tasksCompleted)
• Receives the number of completed tasks.
• Calculates the performance score by multiplying the tasks completed by 10.
• Returns the calculated score.
void reviseTasks(int tasksCompleted)
• Receives the number of completed tasks.
• Increases the received value by 5.
• Prints the revised number of tasks.
void displayResult(int score, int originalTasks)
• Prints the performance score.
• Prints the original number of completed tasks.
Class: EmployeePerformance
The EmployeePerformance class should:
1. Read the number of tasks completed as an integer.
2s Call calculateScore() and store its returned value.
3. Call reviseTasks() with the original task count.
4. Call displayResult() with the calculated score and the original task count.
Input Format
• The input consists of a single integer representing the number of tasks completed by the employee.
Output Format
• Print the output in the following format:
Revised Tasks: <value>
Performance Score: <value>
Original Tasks: <value>*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class EmployeePerformance {
 
    static int calculateScore(int tasksCompleted) {
        return tasksCompleted * 10;
    }
 
    static void reviseTasks(int tasksCompleted) {
        tasksCompleted += 5;
        System.out.println("Revised Tasks: " + tasksCompleted);
    }
 
    static void displayResult(int score, int originalTasks) {
        System.out.println("Performance Score: " + score);
        System.out.println("Original Tasks: " + originalTasks);
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int tasks = sc.nextInt();
        int score = calculateScore(tasks);
        reviseTasks(tasks);
        displayResult(score, tasks);
        sc.close();
    }
}
